hed automatically every 5 minutes."}},"Collection":{"info":"Collection","Rubbing":{"info":"Fish Print","2436046":{"QR":18720,"ToolTip":"[Common Carp]\\r\\nCommon Carp can vary wildly in size. This one is unusually large. Applying ink to the fish and pressing it against paper allows you to preserve a 'fish print', to mark your accomplishment.\\r\\n"},"2436047":{"QR":18721,"ToolTip":"[Percula Clownfish]\\r\\nThe Percula Clownfish is a saltwater fish that can be found in the Indian Ocean near Africa, as well as around Japan and Jeju Island. The larger it is, the more aggressive and difficult to catch it becomes.\\r\\n"},"2436048":{"QR":18722,"ToolTip":" [Halfmoon Betta]\\r\\n Betta are short in length and feature a very long fin. They live in small rivers or ponds. Their unique labyrinth organ makes it possible for them to live in waters with little oxygen.\\r\\n "},"2436049":{"QR":18723,"ToolTip":"[Arowana]\\r\\n These fish grow to be between 50-120 cm long, and flat on their side. They're is popular as aquarium fish due to their multi-colored scales.\\r\\n"},"2436050":{"QR":18724,"ToolTip":"[Blue Sea Slug]\\r\\nThis small slug is around 30-40 mm in size and can be found in tropical oceans. It uses natural camouflage to hide from predators.\\r\\n"},"2436051":{"QR":18725,"ToolTip":"[Dumbo Octopus]\\r\\nLittle is known about the Dumbo Octopus. Beware, as it is rumored to be quite ferocious.\\r\\n"},"2436052":{"QR":18726,"ToolTip":"[Footballfish]\\r\\nThe Footballfish lives in depths up to 10,000m. It may be small, but it has a bizarre appearance and swims slowly.\\r\\n"},"2436053":{"QR":18727,"ToolTip":"[Blue Parrotfish]\\r\\nThe Blue Parrotfish is a rare fish found in the Atlantic. It is so called because it has a face of a parrot.\\r\\n"},"2436054":{"QR":18728,"ToolTip":"[Apple Snail]\\r\\nThe Apple Snail collects moss with its yellow shell. Once it finds a hiding place, it tends to stay hidden. \\r\\n"},"2436055":{"QR":18729,"ToolTip":"[Transparent Fish]\\r\\nKnown only as the Transparent Fish, this creature is completely see-through except for its organs. Little is known about its habits.\\r\\n"}}}}